Thank you for submitting Kestrel Facilities Management Ltd's supplier registration. We've reviewed everything and we're nearly there - we just need the following before we can set you up for payment:

1. Your certificate of insurance expired on 31 March 2026. Please send the current (renewed) certificate.
   Why we need this: Our policy requires current liability insurance for suppliers working on-site or providing services.

2. Your bank letter shows the account is held by 'Kestrel Group Holdings Ltd', but the company being registered is 'Kestrel Facilities Management Ltd' (the form listed the holder as the registering company). We can only pay into an account held by the contracting legal entity. Please either send a bank letter for an account in the name of Kestrel Facilities Management Ltd, or - if payments should go to a parent or group company - let us know and we'll send our third-party payment authorisation form.
   Why we need this: Paying a different legal entity than the one we contract with is the most common route for invoice fraud.

Everything else in your submission checked out, so we'll only re-check the items above. Please reply to this email with the corrected details or documents, quoting reference SUB-2026-1043, by 15 November 2026.

